SUMMARY:MiM: Day-1 software setup (one time)
DESCRIPTION:One-time account setup. Do it once\, never touch again.\n\nDO
 \n- Create the 4 accounts on annual billing (Riverside Pro\, Descript Cr
 eator\, Transistor Pro\, Calendly Standard).\n- In Riverside\, enable 'E
 xport to Descript' (email Riverside support now if the button is missing
 ).\n- Connect the YouTube channel inside Transistor (document the manual
 -upload fallback if it won't connect).\n- Publish a 60-second TRAILER no
 w and submit the RSS feed to Apple Podcasts Connect and Spotify for Crea
 tors (Apple's and Spotify's podcast submission sites)\, so directory rev
 iew (days\, sometimes weeks) clears well before launch.\n- Run one priva
 te/unlisted end-to-end test episode: Transistor -> confirm Apple/Spotify
  ingest + YouTube auto-post actually fire.\n- Build the Calendly 'Record
 ing' event (75 min\, 15-min buffers\, Riverside link as location\, 3 int
 ake questions)\; confirm the invite carries the link and the prep doc re
 solves view-only.\n- Write the guest prep one-pager (Google Doc\, view-o
 nly).\n- Set up the shared master-asset cloud folder (Drive/Dropbox)\, o
 ne folder per episode.\n- Add both Rich and Carla as admins on each acco
 unt where allowed\; record logins in a credentials note.\n- Confirm edit
 or lanes: Rich owns the cut/multicam/export\; Carla owns clip selection 
 + caption QA + guest-clip send.\n\nRIGHT LOOKS LIKE\n- Accounts live + b
 oth admins\; trailer published and feeds submitted for early review\; pr
 ivate end-to-end publish proven\; YouTube connected\; Calendly + prep do
 c verified\; shared asset folder ready.\n\nHOW-TO GUIDES (plain language
 \, jargon decoded\, each with a chatbot prompt)\n- Day-1 setup\, step by
  step: https://github.com/rwsmith96/mechanisms-in-motion/blob/main/how-t
 o/day1-setup.md\n- All guides: https://github.com/rwsmith96/mechanisms-i
 n-motion/blob/main/how-to/README.md\n\nASSISTANT PROMPT (paste into Clau
 de or ChatGPT for step-by-step help)\nYou are helping run Mechanisms in 
 Motion\, the AES podcast: a remote\, two-host video interview show that 
 turns Amazon's internal operating mechanisms into playbooks any company 
 can use (tagline 'Day 1 Energy for Every Stage of Growth'). Rich owns lo
 gistics\; Carla owns the guest slate. First\, if you can open links\, re
 ad the project spec for full\, current context: https://raw.githubuserco
 ntent.com/rwsmith96/mechanisms-in-motion/main/mim-assistant-context.md a
 nd the project repo: https://github.com/rwsmith96/mechanisms-in-motion .
  The relevant how-to guide(s): https://github.com/rwsmith96/mechanisms-i
 n-motion/blob/main/how-to/day1-setup.md . If you cannot open links\, the
  brief below is self-contained\; use it. Today's step: One-time account 
 setup. Do it once\, never touch again. WHAT TO DO: (1) Create the 4 acco
 unts on annual billing (Riverside Pro\, Descript Creator\, Transistor Pr
 o\, Calendly Standard). (2) In Riverside\, enable 'Export to Descript' (
 email Riverside support now if the button is missing). (3) Connect the Y
 ouTube channel inside Transistor (document the manual-upload fallback if
  it won't connect). (4) Publish a 60-second TRAILER now and submit the R
 SS feed to Apple Podcasts Connect and Spotify for Creators (Apple's and 
 Spotify's podcast submission sites)\, so directory review (days\, someti
 mes weeks) clears well before launch. (5) Run one private/unlisted end-t
 o-end test episode: Transistor -> confirm Apple/Spotify ingest + YouTube
  auto-post actually fire. (6) Build the Calendly 'Recording' event (75 m
 in\, 15-min buffers\, Riverside link as location\, 3 intake questions)\;
  confirm the invite carries the link and the prep doc resolves view-only
 . (7) Write the guest prep one-pager (Google Doc\, view-only). (8) Set u
 p the shared master-asset cloud folder (Drive/Dropbox)\, one folder per 
 episode. (9) Add both Rich and Carla as admins on each account where all
 owed\; record logins in a credentials note. (10) Confirm editor lanes: R
 ich owns the cut/multicam/export\; Carla owns clip selection + caption Q
 A + guest-clip send. DONE WHEN: Accounts live + both admins\; trailer pu
 blished and feeds submitted for early review\; private end-to-end publis
 h proven\; YouTube connected\; Calendly + prep doc verified\; shared ass
 et folder ready. YOUR TASK: We are at STEP 6: Day-1 software setup. Give
  me an ordered runbook with the exact click-path for each task\, the tra
 iler + private-test-episode procedure\, the precise Calendly 'Recording'
  fields\, and the full text of the guest prep one-pager (include a one-l
 ine audio+video reuse consent).\n\nFULL PROJECT (all files + guides): ht
 tps://github.com/rwsmith96/mechanisms-in-motion
