DTSTAMP:20260603T160000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260908T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260908T104500
SUMMARY:MiM: Record Ep05 (guest TBD)
LOCATION:Riverside studio link (paste the persistent studio URL here once
  created)
DESCRIPTION:Mechanisms in Motion\, Episode 05. 105-min block: 15 setup + 
 75 record + 15 buffer. The guest's local track is the one irreplaceable 
 asset\; protect it (upload marshal + archive below).\n\nDO\n- T-minus 5 
 min\, BEFORE the guest joins: both hosts confirm the MV7+ is chosen as t
 he microphone in Riverside's settings (a software pick\, not just pluggi
 ng it in)\, 'separate tracks / local recording' is ON (in Riverside's St
 udio settings\; it saves each person's audio to their own computer as in
 surance)\, and the QuickTime backup is rolling. Fix any before admitting
  the guest.\n- Headphones on for everyone (kills echo).\n- Hit Record\; 
 say the slate ('Episode N\, take 1')\; pause 3 seconds silent for sync.\
 n- Record ~60 min of conversation. If a guest's audio is rough\, ask the
 m live to move closer\, turn off fans/AC\, and put on headphones.\n- UPL
 OAD MARSHAL: one host's only end-of-session job is to watch EVERY track 
 (including the GUEST's) to 100% in the Riverside dashboard. The other ho
 st handles the goodbye. The guest is NOT released until the marshal call
 s 'clear.'\n- If a track is missing or stalls\, do NOT end the call: kee
 p the guest on while it re-uploads\; if it can't\, rebook on the spot wh
 ile you have them.\n- Archive immediately: both QuickTime backups + the 
 Riverside download go to the shared cloud folder 'MiM-EpNN-Guest-YYYY-MM
 -DD/' before any editing.\n\nRIGHT LOOKS LIKE\n- Clean separate local tr
 acks captured\; slate + 3-sec sync pause\; GUEST track confirmed 100% be
 fore release\; Ep05 archived to the shared cloud folder\; edit started w
 ithin 48 hours.\n\nHOW-TO GUIDES (plain language\, jargon decoded\, each
  with a chatbot prompt)\n- Recording run-of-show: https://github.com/rws
 mith96/mechanisms-in-motion/blob/main/how-to/riverside-record.md\n- Your
  free local backup: https://github.com/rwsmith96/mechanisms-in-motion/bl
 ob/main/how-to/quicktime-audio-backup.md\n- Editing afterward: https://g
 ithub.com/rwsmith96/mechanisms-in-motion/blob/main/how-to/descript-edit.
 md\n- All guides: https://github.com/rwsmith96/mechanisms-in-motion/blob
 /main/how-to/README.md\n\nASSISTANT PROMPT (paste into Claude or ChatGPT
  for step-by-step help)\nYou are helping run Mechanisms in Motion\, the 
 AES podcast: a remote\, two-host video interview show that turns Amazon'
 s internal operating mechanisms into playbooks any company can use (tagl
 ine 'Day 1 Energy for Every Stage of Growth'). Rich owns logistics\; Car
 la owns the guest slate. First\, if you can open links\, read the projec
 t spec for full\, current context: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rws
 mith96/mechanisms-in-motion/main/mim-assistant-context.md and the projec
 t repo: https://github.com/rwsmith96/mechanisms-in-motion . The relevant
  how-to guide(s): https://github.com/rwsmith96/mechanisms-in-motion/blob
 /main/how-to/riverside-record.md\; https://github.com/rwsmith96/mechanis
 ms-in-motion/blob/main/how-to/quicktime-audio-backup.md\; https://github
 .com/rwsmith96/mechanisms-in-motion/blob/main/how-to/descript-edit.md . 
 If you cannot open links\, the brief below is self-contained\; use it. T
 oday's step: Mechanisms in Motion\, Episode 05. 105-min block: 15 setup 
 + 75 record + 15 buffer. The guest's local track is the one irreplaceabl
 e asset\; protect it (upload marshal + archive below). WHAT TO DO: (1) T
 -minus 5 min\, BEFORE the guest joins: both hosts confirm the MV7+ is ch
 osen as the microphone in Riverside's settings (a software pick\, not ju
 st plugging it in)\, 'separate tracks / local recording' is ON (in River
 side's Studio settings\; it saves each person's audio to their own compu
 ter as insurance)\, and the QuickTime backup is rolling. Fix any before 
 admitting the guest. (2) Headphones on for everyone (kills echo). (3) Hi
 t Record\; say the slate ('Episode N\, take 1')\; pause 3 seconds silent
  for sync. (4) Record ~60 min of conversation. If a guest's audio is rou
 gh\, ask them live to move closer\, turn off fans/AC\, and put on headph
 ones. (5) UPLOAD MARSHAL: one host's only end-of-session job is to watch
  EVERY track (including the GUEST's) to 100% in the Riverside dashboard.
  The other host handles the goodbye. The guest is NOT released until the
  marshal calls 'clear.' (6) If a track is missing or stalls\, do NOT end
  the call: keep the guest on while it re-uploads\; if it can't\, rebook 
 on the spot while you have them. (7) Archive immediately: both QuickTime
  backups + the Riverside download go to the shared cloud folder 'MiM-EpN
 N-Guest-YYYY-MM-DD/' before any editing. DONE WHEN: Clean separate local
  tracks captured\; slate + 3-sec sync pause\; GUEST track confirmed 100%
  before release\; Ep05 archived to the shared cloud folder\; edit starte
 d within 48 hours. YOUR TASK: We are recording Episode 05 today. Before 
 we start\, quiz me on the record-day non-negotiables (T-minus mic/local-
 recording/QuickTime check\, headphones\, slate + sync pause\, upload mar
 shal confirms the GUEST track to 100% before release\, archive to the sh
 ared folder). After the session\, remind me to archive and to start the 
 edit within 48 hours.\n\nFULL PROJECT (all files + guides): https://gith
 ub.com/rwsmith96/mechanisms-in-motion
